timestamp=2026-11-04T20:05:13.358Z level=INFO run=5e0ff14c message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python << 'PY'\n# So only that batch during the spike window. Also look at dispatches just before/after - any other goods that might have been affected?\n# For example, goods already in storage? But the question says \"expected revenue for July 2023 using the available warehouse and sensor data. Calculate Expected Revenue (PLN) — total value of goods dispatched from the warehouse that reached customers as sales. Goods that were disposed of due to spoilage must not be counted as revenue.\"\n# The key is: which dispatched goods were disposed of due to spoilage? The temperature excursion is a strong trace. Also check if there are other \"unmistakable traces\" - sometimes spoilage might be inferred from other signals, but with the data we have (temp logs, catalog, dispatches), the main suspect is the 18th batch.\n# Let us look at all dispatches more broadly. Are there any other weird patterns? Like very large quantities of frozen goods at odd times? Or multiple dispatches with same timestamp (batch) - yes, the 18th is such a batch.\n# Also look at total revenue if we include everything vs exclude that batch.\nimport pandas as pd\n\ncatalog = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/product_catalog.csv')\ncatalog['unit_price'] = catalog['unit_price'].astype(str).str.replace(',', '.', regex=False).astype(float)\ncatalog['storage_category'] = catalog['storage_category'].str.strip()\ncatalog = catalog.rename(columns={'storage_category': 'category'})\n\ntemps = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/temperature_logs.csv')\ntemps['temperature_c'] = temps['temperature_c'].astype(str).str.replace(',', '.', regex=False).astype(float)\ntemps['timestamp'] = pd.to_datetime(temps['timestamp'])\ntemps['zone'] = temps['zone'].str.strip()\nzone_map = {'frozen': 'Frozen', 'FROZEN': 'Frozen', 'meat': 'Meat', 'MEAT': 'Meat', 'dairy': 'Dairy', 'DAIRY': 'Dairy', 'dry': 'Dry', 'DRY': 'Dry'}\ntemps['zone_norm'] = temps['zone'].map(zone_map).fillna(temps['zone'].str.capitalize())\ntemps = temps.rename(columns={'zone_norm': 'category'})\n\ndispatch = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/warehouse_dispatches.csv')\ndispatch['timestamp'] = pd.to_datetime(dispatch['timestamp'])\ndispatch['product_id'] = dispatch['product_id'].str.strip()\nfor idx, row in dispatch.iterrows():\n    pid = row['product_id']\n    if pid not in catalog['product_id'].values:\n        matches = catalog[catalog['ean_code'].astype(str) == str(pid)]\n        if not matches.empty:\n            dispatch.at[idx, 'product_id'] = matches.iloc[0]['product_id']\n\ndf = dispatch.merge(catalog[['product_id', 'name', 'category', 'unit_price', 'max_safe_temp_c']], on='product_id', how='left')\ndf['revenue'] = df['quantity'] * df['unit_price']\ntotal_all = df['revenue'].sum()\nprint(f'Total revenue if all dispatched are sold: {total_all:.2f}')\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
