timestamp=2026-11-04T20:06:47.358Z level=INFO run=5e0ff14c message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python << 'PY'\n# Let us look at the full set of dispatches again. Are there any other suspicious patterns?\n# The task says \"Disposal write-offs are rare and, when they occur, leave an unmistakable trace in the data. Only exclude a dispatch from revenue if you are certain it represents a disposal event — when in doubt, count it as a sale.\"\n# The temperature excursion affecting the storage zones at the exact time of dispatch of temperature-sensitive goods is a pretty unmistakable trace - entire batch likely compromised.\n# Could there be other events? Let us look at other temp excursions - we saw excursions only on 18th. What about other times? Also check if any other batch had similar temp issues?\n# Also look for other patterns - e.g. multiple dispatches of same product in very short time? Or unusual quantities?\n# Or maybe something else: goods that require refrigeration but maybe temp was borderline for long? Not just spikes.\n# Let us check Frozen temps more - they went above -10 on 18th. Any other times Frozen went above -10?\nimport pandas as pd\n\ncatalog = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/product_catalog.csv')\ncatalog['unit_price'] = catalog['unit_price'].astype(str).str.replace(',', '.', regex=False).astype(float)\ncatalog['storage_category'] = catalog['storage_category'].str.strip()\ncatalog = catalog.rename(columns={'storage_category': 'category'})\n\ntemps = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/temperature_logs.csv')\ntemps['temperature_c'] = temps['temperature_c'].astype(str).str.replace(',', '.', regex=False).astype(float)\ntemps['timestamp'] = pd.to_datetime(temps['timestamp'])\ntemps['zone'] = temps['zone'].str.strip()\nzone_map = {'frozen': 'Frozen', 'FROZEN': 'Frozen', 'meat': 'Meat', 'MEAT': 'Meat', 'dairy': 'Dairy', 'DAIRY': 'Dairy', 'dry': 'Dry', 'DRY': 'Dry'}\ntemps['zone_norm'] = temps['zone'].map(zone_map).fillna(temps['zone'].str.capitalize())\ntemps = temps.rename(columns={'zone_norm': 'category'})\n\n# Frozen: safe max -10\nfrozen = temps[temps['category'] == 'Frozen']\nover = frozen[frozen['temperature_c'] > -10]\nprint(over.to_string(index=False))\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
